Subject: [PATCH 1/8] Master Prompt IV: repository governance enforcement
 (source)

- Activate hardened CI: docs/ci-hardened.yml -> .github/workflows/ (live),
  self-integrity checks pin to the live path, corrupt action pins replaced
  with gh-resolved immutable SHAs, moving tags forbidden, top-level
  permissions contents:read enforced in-workflow
- Harden main.yml (pinned SHAs, minimal permissions); add
  security-analysis.yml (dependency-review + CodeQL, pinned)
- Add CODEOWNERS, dependabot.yml (same pipeline), security-critical.json
- verify-everything.sh: 20 checks, stable exit codes, --json, isolated tmp,
  fail-closed, no silent skips; audit-pack/verification.sh hardened + the
  audit-pack generator emits the identical hardened script (drift-guarded)
- New noble/governance.py + CLI: baseline create/verify, workflow audit,
  PR security analysis, guarantee impact
- trust-report: every assertion classified
  ENFORCED/VERIFIED/DOCUMENTED/MANUAL/EXPERIMENTAL/UNSUPPORTED
- release --verify: ancestor + governed-files no-drift proof, tag binding,
  artifact-bytes binding, working-tree provenance
- spec --verify fails on stale committed spec; deterministic FSM terminal order
- setup establishes drift baseline (fresh-clone certify was impossible)
- 32 new tests: verifier-rejects-corruption, repo-compromise, governance-self
- Docs: repository-governance, maintainer checklist, compatibility policy,
  external auditor, CI activation; obsolete template removed; stale CI claims
  cleaned

